# Owning plan 04-23 (PKG-01, D-39): the ivs_* names the installed consumer's object
# (tests/installed-consumer/main.c) references, read with `nm -P -u` and normalized as
# core-symbols.sh does; gate step pkg-install requires exact equality (pkg-consumer-calls), so a
# load, run or digest call cannot be dropped from the consumer quietly. One name per line. Plan 08-16 adds the four snapshot calls of the fifth replay
# (ivs_machine_snapshot_size, _save and _restore, and the instance-free ivs_snapshot_describe).
ivs_api_version
ivs_machine_cpu_state
ivs_machine_create
ivs_machine_destroy
ivs_machine_info
ivs_machine_load
ivs_machine_peek
ivs_machine_reset
ivs_machine_run
ivs_machine_snapshot_restore
ivs_machine_snapshot_save
ivs_machine_snapshot_size
ivs_machine_state_digest
ivs_machine_stic_state
ivs_machine_storage_requirements
ivs_run_stop_name
ivs_snapshot_describe
ivs_status_name
